    <h1>Plano Plumbers Checked Against the City's Own Contractor Registry (2026)</h1>
    <p class="rv-lead">Plano actually sits on two different kinds of ground: roughly west of the Tollway the foundation is Austin Chalk, a limestone that holds fairly still, while the eastern half of the city — including most of the neighborhoods around Historic Downtown — is Blackland Prairie clay, the same shrink-swell soil that keeps foundation and slab-leak crews busy across the rest of Collin County. That split means a plumber who's mostly quoting spot repairs in a west-side kitchen may be underprepared for a tunneling job under a 1970s slab on the east side. Plano's Building Inspections Department also publishes an official list of registered plumbing contractors, which gave us a rare chance to check a private ranking against a government source rather than relying only on reviews. Of the five companies below, three appear on that public registry with matching addresses and phone numbers; the other two are Plano-based businesses we verified against their own sites and outside listings.</p>
